1 new-2/clean-5 The topic tracks two annual figures—the big four AI hyperscalers' combined data-center capital expenditures for 2026 and for 2027—without naming either as the main figure. A single judged question and ladder cannot cover both years, and selecting one would arbitrarily discard an equally tracked outcome.
2 new-2/clean-8 The topic's outcome tracks both six-year fixed and short-tenor GPU rental rates in calendar 2026 without naming either as the main figure. These are distinct prices and cannot be combined into one ladder or reduced to one without choosing a priority the topic does not provide.
5 new-2/clean-7 The topic does not define one verifiable DRAM contract-price figure: it specifies neither a memory product or price series nor how prices across calendar 2026 should be measured. Its outcome also names shortage duration. Choosing a particular contract-price benchmark or annual aggregation would introduce a tracked quantity not identified in the topic or item.
7 new-2/clean-12 The topic's outcome names several figures—combined NVIDIA chip orders/deployments, total chip orders/deployments, and NVIDIA's share—without identifying one as the main figure tracked. It also covers the two-year period 2026–2027 rather than one fiscal or calendar year, and neither the topic nor the item specifies a publication day for that period's figures.
8 new-2/clean-13 The topic's outcome names two distinct figures—total U.S. federal AI spending obligations for calendar 2026 and potential, not-yet-awarded federal AI contract value—without identifying either as the main tracked figure.
12 new-2/clean-15 The topic's outcome tracks both NVIDIA's standalone CPU revenue in calendar 2026 and confirmation that Vera CPUs have begun commercial shipments, without identifying either as the main figure or event.
14 new-2/clean-16 The tracked Helios deployment capacity covers calendar 2026–2027, not one fiscal or calendar year, and neither the topic nor the item specifies a publication day for that combined figure. The listed disclosures do not establish a dated release that would settle it.
16 new-2/clean-23 The tracked capacity target belongs to Ooredoo's Zankore platform, and the additional GPU-capacity figure belongs to Indosat Ooredoo Hutchison (IOH), not NVDA. These are other companies' own operating figures, not aggregate AI capital spending; their use of Nvidia technology does not make them NVDA figures. The topic does not specify a separate, measurable NVDA accelerator-demand outcome.
17 new-2/clean-22 The tracked outcome is U.S. federal restrictions on open-weight or open-source frontier AI models, a matter not covered by any listed theme. It concerns AI model safety regulation, not chip export controls or AI capital spending; potential effects on NVIDIA’s accelerator demand do not make the regulatory decision a company-specific outcome.
22 new-2/clean-24 The tracked figure covers calendar 2026–2027 rather than one fiscal or calendar year, and neither the topic nor the item supplies a publication date for the resale benchmarks or collateral valuations. The proposed year-end checks are assessment dates, not publication dates, so they do not satisfy the exception for a nonannual period.
24 new-2/clean-26 The tracked custom-ASIC accelerator capacity covers the two-calendar-year period 2026–2027, not one fiscal or calendar year, and neither the topic nor the item gives a publication day for that combined figure. Quarterly disclosures through 2027 do not supply a publication date for the two-year total.
25 new-2/clean-27 The topic names several tracked figures without selecting one main figure: combined GPU-neocloud data-center capex for calendar 2026 and 2027, and the portion spent on NVIDIA GPUs in each year. Its outcome does not identify a single figure and year to judge.
28 new-2/clean-34 The topic names several tracked outcomes without identifying a main one: completion of the Poolside transaction on the reported terms, NVIDIA's disclosed Poolside license payment, its Poolside equity investment, and its cumulative licensing-plus-hire deal spending. These cannot be combined into one judged event or figure.
34 new-2/clean-37 The tracked outcome is HBM capacity per Rubin Ultra GPU at first commercial shipments, not an annual figure. Neither the topic nor the item gives a publication day for the launch specifications: “late 2027” and checks through 2027–2028 do not establish one. Recasting this as a shipment event would change the tracked outcome.
38 new-2/clean-41 The topic's outcome names several tracked outcomes—signature of a definitive agreement, completion or collapse of the acquisition, and final purchase price and consideration—without identifying one as primary. A single judged event or figure cannot be selected without changing what the topic tracks.
